  "decision_summary": "L4 provides strong, structurally relevant intestinal permeability and absorption evidence (nepicastat, lorcaserin, UC-781, domperidone, desloratadine, indapamide) supporting high absorption for the query's lipophilic basic benzimidazole-2-thione scaffold. Combined with uniformly high L1 gold-context F values and L3 oral exposure for a cyclic-thiourea analog, the evidence supports F >= 20%; no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20%. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence due to unquantified first-pass metabolism and solubility."
}

